    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d303">

                <pb facs="0803" n="681" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg681"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr.
                            Palmer.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-05-27"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 27,
                        1889</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to instruction No. 262, of the
                    24th of January, 1888, and to instruction No. 266, of February 11, following, I
                    now transmit a copy of a further letter from Mr. John W. Kane, master of the
                    brig <pb facs="0804" n="682" xml:id="pg682"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">J. W. Parker</hi>, touching’ his claim for the remission
                    of an excess of tonnage dues required of him by the customs authorities at Zaza,
                    Cuba, December 27, 1887.</p>
                <p>The Department will be glad to hear what action has been taken in the case, and
                    the result thereof.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d303-a1.xml" xpointer="d303-a1"/>
            </div>
